# Sanity rules

Doc: `docs/CONTENT-MODEL.md`. The Studio in `apps/studio` is provided and validated (0 errors, 0 warnings). **Do not redesign the schema.**

- Content only: `siteSettings`, `uiStrings`, `vehicleClass`, `page`. Zones, prices, hourly rates, extras, vehicles and bookings never go in Sanity.
- `vehicleClass.key` equals `vehicle_classes.key` in Postgres. It is lowercase and unique. A class that exists on one side only is reported (admin warning and build log), not silently skipped.
- Document IDs use hyphens, never dots. Singletons have fixed IDs (`siteSettings`, `uiStrings`).
- Queries use `defineQuery` from `groq`, live in `src/lib/sanity/queries.ts`, project only the fields used, and run with perspective `published`.
- Run `pnpm --filter @tem/studio typegen` after any query or schema change; commit the generated types.
- `uiStrings` keys are listed in `docs/CONTENT-MODEL.md`. A missing key falls back to the code default and logs a build warning.
- Portable Text is rendered with the official renderer; no `set:html` of editor content.
- The dataset is `production`. If it is private, the site reads with `SANITY_READ_TOKEN` at build time only.
- Seed content is DEMO. Real content replaces it before launch.
